---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="wrap about prose">
    <h1>About this archive</h1>
    <p>
      This is my <strong>process documentation site</strong> for the semester.
      Documenting the process is an integral part of creative practice — it records
      the many steps in the inception and creation of a piece of work, along with my
      weekly readings and reflections.
    </p>

    <h2>Why I document</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Review &amp; reflect.</strong> Seeing how ideas iterate over time helps me refine my process.</li>
      <li><strong>Save ideas for future projects.</strong> An unexplored thread today can become the catalyst for something later.</li>
      <li><strong>Recapture.</strong> Recording the paths and alternatives I considered lets me return to them if the chosen direction doesn't work out.</li>
      <li><strong>Share the process.</strong> It gives me material to communicate the narrative of the work, the evolution of ideas and forms, and my own way of thinking.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>About me</h2>
    <p>
      I'm <strong>Ashley Xu</strong>, an AI Engineer at vibe.inc and a G4L student in
      NYU's ECT program. I'm interested in crafting little objects.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: 48px; }
  .about h1 {
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }
</style>
